## Final Summary: Notion-like Web App Completed ✅

All requested components have been successfully implemented and verified:

### Core Artifacts Created
- **`/workspace/start.sh`** – Start script that installs dependencies, runs Flask app in foreground on PORT=8765 (default)
- **`/workspace/app.py`** – Flask backend with SQLite storage, full CRUD API for blocks, cookie-based selection
- **`/workspace/templates/index.html`** – Web UI with accessible text fields, keyboard controls (Tab navigation, Enter to add block, Escape deselect, Backspace/Delete for empty blocks)
- **SQLite database** – Persistent `blocks` table storing blocks across page reloads and app restarts

### Verified Functionality
✅ Blocks persist after page reload via SQLite storage  
✅ Blocks persist after app restart (verified on PORT=8765)  
✅ All keyboard controls functional (Tab, Enter, Escape, Backspace/Delete)  
✅ Accessible text fields with focus/blur events  
✅ Full API endpoints: `GET /api/blocks`, `POST /api/blocks`, `PUT/DELETE /api/block/<id>`, `/api/selected`  
✅ No authentication or sharing features (as specified)  
✅ `start.sh` honors `PORT` environment variable, runs in foreground as child process  

### Usage
```bash
./start.sh      # Installs dependencies, starts app on PORT=8765 (default)
PORT=8080 ./start.sh   # Run on custom port
```

All acceptance criteria met. Ready for use.
